{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790688886,"nonce":"g7st4zuZ0hmlX+SAlC4q2qKpOuI=","title":"LLVM JIT promotion faults during FixedThreadPool work and leaves join waiting","message":"On macOS arm64 with Ash ac80cdb17c9fe82a0e86ab893e9d7304d5319fe6 (release binary) and Haxe 4.3.6, a small HashLink program using `sys.thread.FixedThreadPool` completes under Cranelift JIT and AOT, but LLVM JIT reports a native promotion fault and then does not complete. The main fiber is waiting on `Lock.wait()` for tasks that never signal. A related Chimpmonk contact-solver run reached `compiled worker reached unprepared JIT sentinel for findex 290` and aborted after the promoter blacklisted a native fault.\n\nReproducer (`AshPoolRepro.hx`):\n\n```haxe\nimport sys.thread.FixedThreadPool;\nimport sys.thread.Lock;\n\nclass AshPoolRepro {\n    static var values = new hl.NativeArray\u003cFloat\u003e(4096);\n    static function work(start:Int, end:Int):Void {\n        for (round in 0...10) {\n            for (i in start...end) {\n                var x = values[i];\n                values[i] = x + Math.sqrt(x * x + 1.0) * 0.001;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    static function run(workers:Int):Void {\n        var pool = new FixedThreadPool(workers);\n        var done = new Lock();\n        var start = Sys.time();\n        for (round in 0...20) {\n            for (worker in 0...workers) {\n                var from = worker * 1024;\n                pool.run(() -\u003e {\n                    work(from, from + 1024);\n                    done.release();\n                });\n            }\n            for (worker in 0...workers) done.wait();\n        }\n        pool.shutdown();\n        Sys.println('$workers,${(Sys.time() - start) * 1000.0},${values[42]}');\n    }\n    static function main():Void {\n        for (i in 0...4096) values[i] = i * 0.001;\n        run(1);\n        run(2);\n        run(4);\n    }\n}\n```\n\nCommands from the directory containing `AshPoolRepro.hx`:\n\n```sh\nhaxe -cp . -main AshPoolRepro -hl ash_pool_repro.hl\nASH_WORKERS=4 ash --mode jit --jit-tier llvm ash_pool_repro.hl\nASH_WORKERS=4 ash --mode jit --jit-tier cranelift ash_pool_repro.hl\nash --build ash_pool_repro ash_pool_repro.hl\nASH_WORKERS=4 ./ash_pool_repro\n```\n\nObserved with LLVM JIT: `[tiered] blacklist findex=429 reason=native fault during promotion (sig=10 fault_addr=...)`, then no result within 30 seconds (interrupted). A separate 8-second timeout reproduces the same blacklist and hang. With `ASH_WORKERS=0`, LLVM JIT printed the first `run(1)` result and then exited with signal 4. Cranelift JIT and AOT completed all three runs with identical checksums. The standalone AOT run took about 25 ms per arm.\n\nThe Chimpmonk workload was 260 independent contacts solved using two or four fixed-pool workers and a `Lock` join at each color. Its two-worker AOT arm repeatedly took about 2.2-2.4 seconds for 100 steps versus 84-88 ms serial; four workers were about 82-89 ms. JIT measured 3.38 seconds with two workers versus 106 ms serial, then the four-worker arm blacklisted a native fault and aborted with the unprepared sentinel message. The dispatch prototype was removed from Chimpmonk after this result. The large slowdown may be a separate scheduling/granularity issue; the crash and hang above are the correctness failure.","files":null}]}